> The easiest way to do this is to forget username /
> passwords completly 
> and use ssh keys for authentication.
> This is really easy :
> 
> First run ssh-keygen   on the source machine to
> generate your PUBLIC key
> (give blank passphrase when asked)
> Then, add your public key which you just created to
> the end of the 
> .ssh/authorized_keys file on the TARGET machine.
> 
> hey presto ! No password problems, and completly
> secure logins using 
> key based authentication !
> 
> Do a google search for ssh-keygen, or a  man ssh
