After sending the post, I did finally find that buried the Tru64 SPD is
the part numbers for ordering the source license.  David Pushee and David
DeWolfe both emailed them to me as well.  

The answer is yes, they are still available, provided you can satisfy SCO
that you are licensed.  My current problem is that SCO inherited our
license from Novell and seems to think we are only registered for
version 3.0, whereas we need 4.2.  I do have a license from Novell for
that verison, so now I have to convince SCO that that is valid so they can
give the ok to HP.

Here are the part numbers for anyone interested:

QB-6ADBA-E8   Tru64 UNIX EDU SRC LIC/CD                                         
QB-6ADBE-E8   Tru64 UNIX ED UP SRC LIC/CD                                       
                                                                                
QB-6ADAA-E8   Tru64 UNIX SRC LIC/CD                                             
